# egui desktop (Construct / Car)

Toolkit is **egui** via **eframe** on the shared `mde-egui` DRM/GBM + libinput
harness. There is no Wayland compositor and no native host app. Surfaces are
panels inside the one shell (`mde-shell-egui`), not separate clients.

## Look source

Use `mde-egui` `Style` / `Motion` / `Fonts` / `widgets`. Do not hand-roll
colors, durations, or hover text.

```rust
// BAD — style leak (fails install-helpers/lint-style-leaks.sh)
ui.colored_label(Color32::from_rgb(0x39, 0x39, 0x39), "Peers");
ui.animate_bool_with_time(id, open, 0.12);

// GOOD — shared tokens
ui.colored_label(style.text_secondary, "Peers");
let t = motion.animate_bool(ui, id, open);
```

Run `install-helpers/lint-style-leaks.sh` after UI edits. New glyphs go through
the shared icon registry (`lint-carbon-icon-registry.py`).

## Interface locks

- Exactly two interfaces: **Construct** and **Car**
  (`docs/design/platform-interfaces.md`).
- Construct taskbar is full-width, 48px, icon-only Start/Search + Back + Home,
  user-managed centered pins, placement control on the right. Start opens
  Front Door search — not a Start menu. Do not add tray flyouts or a second
  launcher.
- Icon V2: app/service/role icons are simple linework, ≤3 product colors, no
  plates. Toolbar/action/status icons stay monochrome and semantic-colored.
- Motion lives in `mde-egui` (MOTION-DRM). No per-widget timing literals.
- Accessibility is deferred for the 12.0 cutover — not a DoD gate.

## Boundaries

- Guest Chromium owns Browser chrome. Construct styles only
  connection / unavailable / diagnostic frames around the typed `browser-vm`
  session. Do not wrap or restyle guest pixels.
- New UI is glue over existing crates. Shell must not depend outward
  (`lint-layered-tiers.sh`).
- Do not polish or revive iced / libcosmic / `mde-workbench` code.

Visual `/preview` captures are optional and never a blocker. GUI/runtime claims
need farm verification or an explicit note that live hardware was unavailable.
